  "description": "Reid Let’s MTB | Electric mountain bike\nBuilt for trail adventures and varied terrain – the Reid Let’s MTB combines electric assistance, confident handling and reliable components for off-road riding.\nThe Reid Let’s MTB is designed for riders looking to explore trails, tackle climbs and enjoy longer rides with the support of electric assistance. Its 29-inch 6061 alloy frame features internal cable routing and an integrated 360Wh battery, creating a clean design with balanced handling on and off the trails.\nA 250W Ananda rear hub motor provides pedal assistance across five levels, helping you tackle inclines and cover more ground. The Ananda D19 handlebar-mounted display features Bluetooth connectivity and app compatibility, keeping essential ride information within easy reach.\nThe Uding D6 suspension fork offers 100mm of travel to help absorb bumps, roots and uneven surfaces, while the Shimano rear derailleur and L-TWOO 7-speed trigger shifter provide straightforward gearing for climbs and descents. Tektro HDM275 hydraulic disc brakes, with a 180mm front rotor and 160mm rear rotor, deliver controlled stopping power across varied riding conditions.\nLarge 29-inch wheels fitted with Wanda 29 x 2.25-inch tyres provide traction, stability and the ability to roll over trail obstacles. An oversized 700mm alloy riser bar and 60mm alloy stem support confident handling, while the MTB comfort saddle and rubber grips add comfort on longer rides.\nWith its suspension fork, capable wheel setup and electric assistance, the Let’s MTB is built for riders who want to explore off-road routes and enjoy a little extra support on the way.\nThe Let’s MTB is ideal for:\n\nTrail riding and off-road adventures, with a suspension fork and grippy 29-inch tyres\n\nRiders tackling hills and varied terrain, with a 250W rear hub motor and five levels of assistance\n\nRiders looking for stable handling, with a 29-inch wheel setup and 6061 alloy frame\n\nComfortable trail riding, with 100mm of front suspension travel to help absorb bumps and uneven surfaces\n\nReliable braking on varied terrain, with Tektro hydraulic disc brakes and front and rear rotors\n\nRiders who want straightforward gearing, with a 7-speed drivetrain for climbs and descents\n\nLonger outdoor rides, with an integrated 360Wh battery and a Bluetooth-compatible display\n\nPlease make sure to familiarise yourself with eBike safety information before charging or using your new Reid. You can view and download user manuals and safety instructions here.",
